From adcb53459ca9fabaa0c457231cd56dbd8b789698 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 15:39:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: find the first empty pack slot when the pack is empty

borg_first_empty_inventory_slot() scans down from the last pack slot for
the last used one and returns the slot after it.  With an empty pack the
loop finds no used slot and the function returned -1, which every caller
reads as "no room in the pack".

So a Borg with nothing in its pack refused every purchase and every
take from the home.  A starving character in town with gold and food on
sale in the General Store did not set out to buy the food.

Let the loop leave i at -1 for an empty pack and return the slot after
the last used one, which is slot 0 in that case.

Tracked as diegoami/neo-angband-tracker#60.
---
 src/borg/borg-inventory.c | 10 ++++++----
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-inventory.c b/src/borg/borg-inventory.c
index 7f39ec3a0..72a1c5275 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-inventory.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-inventory.c
@@ -256,12 +256,14 @@ int borg_first_empty_inventory_slot(void)
 {
     int i;
 
+    /* Find the last used slot (-1 when the pack is empty) */
     for (i = PACK_SLOTS - 1; i >= 0; i--)
-        if (borg_items[i].iqty) {
-            if ((i + 1) < PACK_SLOTS)
-                return i + 1;
+        if (borg_items[i].iqty)
             break;
-        }
+
+    /* The slot after it is the first empty one, if the pack has room */
+    if ((i + 1) < PACK_SLOTS)
+        return i + 1;
 
     return -1;
 }
